+## Session 62: unblinding the narrow-fact dataflow — the -g directive blindness
+
+<!-- src: engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-22D-dataflow-unblind-and-pair-fold.md -->
+
+**The census argument is closed.** After S06's narrow-compare folds, the
+remaining boot-code gap is one defect class with a number on it:
+cpucheck.c is lccc 350 insns vs gcc 157 with **movz* at parity (1/1)** —
+the residue is 43 slot-stores + 30 slot-loads + 14 relay movls where gcc
+emits zero. Store-to-frame corpus-wide: 515 vs 46. It is all register
+residency now.
+
+**Two blind spots fixed in `eliminate_redundant_zext_i686`** (the
+whole-function is_byte/is_16 dataflow):
+
+1. `LineKind::Directive` sat in `is_barrier()`, and with `-g` the emitter
+   writes a `.loc` per statement — the dataflow wiped every fact at every
+   statement boundary and never accumulated across one. The same
+   REG_NONE fallthrough hit `invalidates_all_narrow_facts`' fail-closed
+   arm. The law now written down: **a directive emits no instruction, so
+   it fences nothing**; labels/calls/jumps/returns/inline-asm stay
+   barriers. The x86-64 `redundant_ext.rs` already had this right.
+2. `andl $imm` reassigned facts from the immediate's range. But AND only
+   clears bits — a narrow value stays narrow under every mask. The law is
+   now monotone (`fact = fact || imm_covers_range`), which is what lets
+   video-mode.c's `andl $-32769` keep `is_16` and its trailing
+   `movzwl %ax,%eax` finally die.
+
+Boot corpus: **5460 → 5442 insns, 24368 → 24290 B** (gcc 3461/14270).
+Unit 3191/0; CI 60/0; QEMU 16/16, zero serial noise; gate 28928.
+
+**Landed** `fold_zext_pair_reg_compare` (CCC_NO_ZEXT_PAIR_CMP_FOLD):
+`movz/sext S1,%A; movz/sext S2,%B; cmpl %A,%B; jcc/setcc` → one
+`cmp{b,w}` with memory sources substituted verbatim. Flag law pinned at
+the wrap rows: signed readers refuse zext/zext (top-bit rows disagree);
+sext/sext folds everything (sext is monotone in both orders); mixed
+refuses. Fires zero times in this boot corpus — its one candidate is a
+`jl` reader and the refusal is correct — kept for the shapes the RA work
+will surface; the runtime guard drives the shape end-to-end
+(EXPECT_A 569 → 683).
+
+**RA evidence locked for next session** (`LCCC_DBG_RA check_cpuflags`):
+values=22 assigned=10; the pool (r0/r1/r2/r3/r5/r6) is spent on long
+low-use ranges allocated by **start-point order**, while short hot values
+(`v10 [8,10] uses=10`, `v13`, `v16`, `v21`) sit in slots *marked
+elig=true*. Next move: spill-cost-ordered allocation + second-chance
+eviction, canonical repro = cpucheck's loop accumulator (`orl $130,%ebx`
+in gcc vs lccc's five-line staging). S59's falsification
+(CCC_NO_I686_ACCUM_NOHOME, +391 B) rules out the naive flip; this is an
+allocation-order defect, not a policy defect.
+
+## Session 62 (cont): the S06 flag-law correction accepted, and the harness-choke fix
+
+**Upstream `adace81a` corrected the S06 immediate-fold law, and the
+critique is right — recorded here because the wrong proof is in this
+journal one entry above.** `cmpb $50,K` with K=200: the 8-bit subtraction
+yields 0x96 — SF=1, OF=0 (−56 − 50 = −106 fits the signed byte range, so
+no overflow) — while the 32-bit view of `cmpl $50,%r` over `zext(K)`
+yields SF=0, OF=0. `jl` therefore *diverges*: the two views do NOT agree
+on signed readers once K can exceed 127. My "SF and OF are set together
+at the wrap rows" claim was false, and the S06 guard missed it because
+its signed readers went through `movsbl` sources, which the fold refuses.
+Accepted upstream's `flags_reader_window_ok` (veto every reader outside
+the ZF/CF-safe sets across the whole flags-live window — sound because
+it is conservative in the reader set, not the value set). The
+session-62 **pair** fold was derived against the corrected law from the
+start: zext/zext refuses signed readers; sext/sext folds every reader
+(sign extension is monotone in both orders and the w-bit subtraction
+computes the signed comparison of its operands by definition); mixed
+refuses outright.
+
+**Root cause of the recurring environment wipes found and fixed.** The
+turn-end workspace snapshot caps around 128 MB / 10k files over
+`/home/user`; sessions were ending with ~2.5 GB in it (≈1 GB rustup in
+`.rustup`/`.cargo`, ≈1.4 GB built kernel tree, `.git`, build junk), the
+snapshot scan choked ("Scanning workspace…"), and the restore came back
+from a truncated checkpoint — dropping the toolchain, `.git`, and the
+kernel tree every time. The fix is structural: all heavy regenerable
+state now lives under `~/target/…` (directory names `target` are
+excluded from snapshots) — `target/rustup`, `target/cargo`,
+`target/kernel-work` — wired through `.profile` (RUSTUP_HOME/CARGO_HOME/
+KERNEL_DIR) and the default paths of all twelve kernel tooling scripts.
+The persisted workspace is now ~15 MB and the toolchain/kernel re-bootstrap
+is scripted and deterministic.
+
+## Session 63: the entry-gate trap, the terminal sweep, and the zero-test fold
+
+**Landed** `fold_logical_zero_test` (CCC_NO_LOGICAL_TEST_FOLD): deletes
+the zero-test after a logical op on the same register — `and|or|xor
+SRC,%R; cmpl $0,%R | test %Rn,%Rn` → drop the second line. The flag law
+needs **no reader gate at all** (the only such fold in the file): a
+logical op clears CF/OF and sets ZF/SF/PF from its result — exactly what
+`cmpl $0` over that result produces. The width law does the work the
+reader law does elsewhere: the test must read exactly the flagged bits
+(`testl` after 32-bit ops, same-width narrow self-test after andw/andb;
+a wider test reads unflagged upper bits — refused, pinned).
+
+**The placement lesson — an architectural finding, not a one-off.** The
+shape's window is opened by *other* passes: the raw stream is
+`andl $1,%eax; movl %eax,%esi; testl %esi,%esi` (a staging copy between);
+`fold_reg_copy_idioms` (Phase 3.8) owns the copy-crossing rewrite,
+`propagate_reg_copies` retargets the reader, Phase 4's liveness pass
+deletes the dead copy. My first three wirings (global site, changed2
+fixpoint, inside the phase-3.8 loop) all stayed dormant on the real
+pipeline — the last because **phase 3.8's fixpoint has an entry gate**
+(`changed8` initialized from three other folds) and never executes for
+functions whose gate folds all decline: 11 boot-corpus sites survived
+exactly this way while every unit test on hand-written final text passed.
+The fix is an unconditional **terminal direct-window sweep** (this fold +
+the zext-pair fold) after the phase 3.8 block and again before Phase 6
+renders — legal because neither fold orphans a value, so no re-fixpoint.
+Rule for the future: **a pass whose window other passes open must run
+unconditionally at a pipeline point after the last window-opener, not
+only inside another pass's gated fixpoint.** (Diagnosis made fast by
+`LCCC_DEBUG_PEEPHOLE_IN` + a temp env-gated trace — both worth keeping in
+mind before touching driver wiring blind.)
+
+Boot corpus: **5449 → 5438 insns, 24121 → 24100 B**. Unit 3227/0. Also
+this session: the zext-pair fold's reader gate now vets the WHOLE
+flags-live window (the adace81a law — a second reader `je`-then-`jl`
+binds exactly like a lone `jl`; four new pins), closing a soundness gap
+the S62 pair pass inherited from the pre-correction imm-fold law.
+
+## Session 63 (cont.): the workqueue.o ICE — alias-aware home freshness
+
+Upstream's kernel gate was BROKEN: every full kernel build from current
+main died at `kernel/workqueue.o` with the operand_to_rax hard gate
+("value 103 ... register home is stale (clobbered) with no slot/remat/
+acc recovery"). Diagnosis ladder that got there in one session: (1)
+proved my commits innocent by rebuilding the pre-change binary in a
+worktree and reproducing identically; (2) killed the source-shrink path
+early — ddmin showed the trigger is module-order dependent (any
+deletion shifts value ids and hides it) — and pivoted to flag matrix
+(-O1 clean, -O2 fires regardless of modulo-sched) + the built-in
+CCC_DEBUG_NOHOME diagnostic; (3) the NOHOME line said everything:
+`home=Some(3) fresh=false sharers=[107,109,103,265] defined_by=None` —
+a phi-coalesced induction chain (v107→v109→v103) homed slot-less in
+r13, whose in-place chain update (`cmovnel`) freshens only the newest
+id and evicts the older SAME-VALUE ids. The freshness map tracks SSA
+ids; coalescing made one logical value wear four of them. The hard gate
+was RIGHT to refuse; the bookkeeping was what couldn't see the
+equivalence.
+
+Fix (7308462f): publish the allocator's blessed same-value classes —
+exactly the set the overlap verifier unions (slot-coalesce webs +
+APPLIED phi destructive updates + FP webs) — as
+`RegAllocResult::phi_chain`, and make all six read-side freshness gates
+alias-aware (`home_readable_via_alias`): a clobbered mark is readable
+when a non-clobbered class sibling shares the register. Write-side
+accounting untouched; non-alias-aware targets get an empty map and
+bit-identical behavior. Lesson for the roadmap: RA-3 (pressure-aware
+greedy scan) and any future coalescer MUST keep feeding this map — the
+verifier's blessed classes and the emitter's alias map must stay the
+same set or the gate starts refusing values that exist.
+
+Also learned the hard way: `ci_local.sh` and `build_kernel_vm.sh`
+MUST NOT run concurrently — CI's cargo rebuild replaces
+target/fastbuild/lccc while make is exec'ing it (first "failure" was
+exactly that, the second was the real ICE). Serial gates from now on.
+
+Validation: isolated workqueue.o compile clean (first time since
+adace81a); full bzImage build KBUILD-EXIT=0; QEMU boot 16/16; unit
+3228/0; boot census 5021 vs 5032 fold-off (−11 = the 11 zero-test
+sites, against the regenerated-tree baseline gcc 3183).
